## Cores
C1 CLOCK — rho(z), the terminal bound rho_inf, the inversion z(ln rho).
C2 SEAT — today's address (E, split, I) from (M, rho) alone.
C3 SWEEP — the STEP trajectory from recombination to the terminal state.
C4 EDGEWATCH — the crossing solver: for each filed edge, the exact epoch
the trajectory crosses it, or NEVER (beyond the terminal bound).
C5 ROSTER — the four closing epochs seated on the planet's own trajectory.
C6 LEDGER — emits the blueprint: transitions ordered by epoch, each with
its kind, its edge, the planet's full state at the crossing, and its
standing against the formation class epoch (z ~ 0.43, canon class label;
deeper crossings are the register's pre-history, flagged on the face).

